<title>GREECE: ATHLETICS-PROFILE OF WORLD TRIPLE JUMP CHAMPION KASPARKOVA.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-PROFILE OF WORLD TRIPLE JUMP CHAMPION KASPARKOVA.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of Sarka Kasparkova, who won the world women's triple jump final on Monday.</p>
<p>Born May 20, 1971. Karvina, Czech Republic.</p>
<p>Took bronze at the 1996 Atlanta Olympics and again at last March's indoor world championships in Paris.</p>
<p>Improved her personal best by over 20 centimetres in the Monday's final, recording the third longest jump ever of 15.20 metres.</p>
</text>
